---
import "../styles/study.css";
import "../styles/direction.css";

const tokens = [
  [
    "Type families",
    "Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif. Consolas / Liberation Mono for actual code and item identifiers only.",
  ],
  [
    "Body and captions",
    "17px / 1.55, weight 400; supporting captions 14px / 1.5. Paragraph measure capped at 61ch.",
  ],
  [
    "Headings",
    "H1 clamp(42px, 5.7vw, 80px); H2 clamp(32px, 3.5vw, 48px). Weight 500, line-height 1.04, tracking −0.045em. H3 24px / 1.15, tracking −0.025em. Arial resolves 500 to its available regular face.",
  ],
  [
    "Wordmark",
    "24px, weight 700, tracking −0.06em. The name itself forms the mark.",
  ],
  [
    "Color roles",
    "White #FFFFFF ground; #181818 primary text and action; #5B5B5B secondary text; #F0F0F0 evidence field; #C7C7C7 nonessential grouping rules. No accent hue in the interface.",
  ],
  [
    "Spacing",
    "4px base. Use 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64, 80, 96 and 128px. Section separation clamp(64px, 7vw, 104px).",
  ],
  [
    "Page geometry",
    "1320px maximum width including gutters. Gutters clamp(24px, 4.5vw, 64px). Intro columns 1.5:1; software feature 0.7:1.3; hardware 0.8:1.2.",
  ],
  [
    "Responsive behavior",
    "At 900px, reduce large column gaps to 40px. At 620px, use one column, 24px gutters, and a visible wrapping navigation row. Introduce the offer and inquiry action before the evidence.",
  ],
  [
    "Links and actions",
    "Underline text links; primary action is solid ink with white text and a 2px radius. Hover #5B5B5B; pressed #454545. Minimum 44px height for standalone links, 48px for the primary action.",
  ],
  [
    "Focus and motion",
    "2px #181818 focus outline, offset 4px. Static content appears immediately. Only 150ms interaction color feedback; reduced-motion removes transitions and smooth scrolling.",
  ],
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Recommended visual direction and exact specifications from the Thread & Signal homepage studies."
    />
    <title>Visual direction | Thread &amp; Signal</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="direction page-width">
      <a class="text-link" href="/">Open the current homepage</a>
      <p class="caption">
        Earlier direction. Superseded by the current work-led homepage after
        review.
      </p>
      <header>
        <p class="project-kind">Thread &amp; Signal · September 13, 2026</p>
        <h1>Let the work<br />give the site its identity.</h1>
        <p class="direction-lead">
          Recommended: the portfolio opening, with a direct offer, readable
          software evidence, and actual objects.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/portfolio/"
          >Open the recommended composition →</a
        >
      </header>

      <section aria-labelledby="choice">
        <h2 id="choice">Why this composition</h2>
        <p>
          The portfolio opening makes the custom software offer and the person
          behind it clear before asking a visitor to interpret an experiment.
          The software test, enclosure render, assembly photograph, and release
          records each have a different job and a proportion suited to their
          content.
        </p>
        <p>
          The case-study opening explains how an assessment can identify a
          result that should not ship. It is a useful structure for a project
          detail page. As the homepage, however, it makes one failed evaluation
          dominate the practice before a visitor sees the rest of the work.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a design recommendation based on the rendered studies, not a
          measured conversion result or a decision already approved by visitors.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="structure">
        <h2 id="structure">The page has a deliberate sequence</h2>
        <ol class="direction-sequence">
          <li>
            <strong>Offer and author.</strong> Custom software for recurring work;
            local AI explained in the accompanying sentence. A visible invitation
            to discuss a workflow.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>One software example.</strong> A readable inventory table with
            the failed check beside it. The table is an explanation of the documented
            test, not a simulated product interface.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A physical object.</strong> The enclosure render shows the exterior;
            a smaller photograph shows the board and heatsink inside. Captions distinguish
            CAD from photography.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A short process record.</strong> Request, checks, and release
            form a real three-step sequence across the page, then stack on mobile.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A practical engagement.</strong> What to bring, what the assessment
            covers, and what the visitor receives. Then a short introduction to Charles
            and a direct contact invitation.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="specification">
        <h2 id="specification">Exact visual specification</h2>
        <p>
          These values are implemented in the studies. The interface can remain
          black and white in the next iteration; restore the original colors of
          genuine photographs when developing the selected homepage. Color in a
          real object conveys material information.
        </p>
        <dl class="direction-tokens">
          {
            tokens.map(([name, value]) => (
              <div>
                <>
                  <dt>{name}</dt>
                  <dd>{value}</dd>
                </>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="evidence">
        <h2 id="evidence">Evidence is part of the design</h2>
        <p>
          The Animus Ferric example is the recorded August 26, 2026 evaluation
          of Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct Q4_K_M. It failed the required output
          contract. Expected quantities remain explicitly labeled; neither study
          presents them as successful model output. The broader evaluation
          completed zero of three task contracts.
        </p>
        <p>
          The enclosure assets come from the public project. The closed design
          is a v2.2 CAD render; the assembly photograph has no verified version
          label. Sprint Loops is illustrated using this website's own recorded
          update. None is presented as a client outcome.
        </p>
        <p>
          For production, generate responsive image sizes, preserve useful
          detail, and link each project to its source and a fuller explanation.
          A successful demonstration would need its own verified record before
          making an outcome claim.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="review">
        <h2 id="review">How this addresses the feedback</h2>
        <p>
          The supplied <a
            href="https://claude.ai/public/artifacts/37cb0fd0-c3a9-457e-bd1b-745a4c1009fa"
            >house-style specimen</a
          > shows why a palette change leaves the same structural habits intact. These
          studies replace decorative technical imagery with evidence, remove repeated
          promotional containers, and use content to determine scale and arrangement.
        </p>
        <p>
          The remaining familiar elements have explicit roles: a table compares
          quantities; a gray field groups one evaluation; small project labels
          identify the work; and three process stages represent an actual
          sequence. Avoid judging the page by counting stylistic markers alone.
        </p>
        <p>
          Useful references were <a href="https://panic.com/"
            >Panic's recognizable products</a
          >, <a href="https://play.date/">Playdate's views of a real object</a>,
          and <a href="https://ciechanow.ski/"
            >Bartosz Ciechanowski's connection between explanations and
            demonstrations</a
          >. Their palettes and page templates are not prescribed here.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="next">
        <h2 id="next">The next implementation boundary</h2>
        <p>
          Use the portfolio composition to develop the production homepage,
          connect the full Work and Writing navigation, restore useful
          photographic color, and integrate the contact route. Then apply the
          resulting system to the remaining pages and update the affected
          regression checks.
        </p>
        <p>
          Review whether visitors can identify the offer, the author, and the
          next step. These local studies establish a reviewable direction; they
          have not been published to the live site.
        </p>
      </section>
      <footer>
        <a class="text-link" href="/comparison/"
          >← Back to the earlier comparison</a
        >
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
